{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    Uses an efficient prefix sum approach by transforming each digit d to d-1.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    prefix_sum = 0\n    # Stores the frequency of each prefix sum encountered.\n    # {0: 1} accounts for the case where a prefix sum of 0 occurs before the first element,\n    # allowing for subarrays starting from index 0.\n    prefix_freq = {0: 1}\n\n    for char_digit in s:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        # Transform digit 'd' to 'd - 1'.\n        # A substring [i, j] satisfies sum(digits) == length\n        # if sum(digits in s[i:j]) - length(s[i:j]) == 0.\n        # This is equivalent to sum((d-1) for d in s[i:j]) == 0.\n        # Using prefix sums, this means prefix_sum[j] - prefix_sum[i-1] == 0,\n        # or prefix_sum[j] == prefix_sum[i-1].\n        transformed_value = digit - 1\n        prefix_sum += transformed_value\n\n        # If the current prefix_sum has been seen before, it means\n        # there are substrings ending at the current position whose transformed sum is 0.\n        count += prefix_freq.get(prefix_sum, 0)\n\n        # Increment the frequency of the current prefix_sum.\n        prefix_freq[prefix_sum] = prefix_freq.get(prefix_sum, 0) + 1\n\n    return count"}
