{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(seq1, seq2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two sequences follow the same structural pattern.\n    The pattern is determined by the first-occurrence index of each unique element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(seq1) != len(seq2):\n        return False\n\n    def _generate_pattern_key(seq):\n        \"\"\"Converts a sequence into a tuple of integers representing its pattern.\"\"\"\n        seen_elements = {}\n        pattern_key = []\n        next_index = 0\n        for element in seq:\n            if element not in seen_elements:\n                seen_elements[element] = next_index\n                next_index += 1\n            pattern_key.append(seen_elements[element])\n        return tuple(pattern_key)\n\n    key1 = _generate_pattern_key(seq1)\n    key2 = _generate_pattern_key(seq2)\n\n    return key1 == key2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "def find_tuples(tuples, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples from a list where all elements are divisible by k.\n    Assumes k is a non-zero integer and tuple elements are integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_tuples = []\n    for current_tuple in tuples:\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        for element in current_tuple:\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n        if all_elements_divisible:\n            filtered_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n    return filtered_tuples"}
