{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the n-th number in the Newman\u2013Conway sequence (1-based index).\n    Example: sequence(10) == 6\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: if n is not an integer >= 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer >= 1\")\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # 1-based array for convenience\n    a = [0] * (n + 1)\n    a[1] = 1\n    a[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        prev = a[i - 1]\n        a[i] = a[prev] + a[i - prev]\n\n    return a[n]"}
