{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "import heapq\ndef larg_nnum(lst: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest unique items from the input list, sorted in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Deduplicate the list to consider only unique items for 'n largest'\n    unique_items = list(set(lst))\n\n    # Use heapq.nlargest to efficiently find the n largest unique items\n    return heapq.nlargest(n, unique_items)"}
