{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest palindromic subsequence (LPS) for a given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time and O(n) space.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp_prev_row[j] will represent LPS length for substring s[i+1..j] in the previous iteration\n    dp_prev_row = [0] * n\n\n    # Iterate start index i from n-1 down to 0\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        dp_current_row = [0] * n\n        dp_current_row[i] = 1  # single character is a palindrome of length 1\n\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # characters match: extend inner palindrome\n                dp_current_row[j] = 2 + (dp_prev_row[j - 1] if j - 1 >= 0 else 0)\n            else:\n                # take max of excluding one end\n                dp_current_row[j] = max(dp_prev_row[j], dp_current_row[j - 1])\n\n        dp_prev_row = dp_current_row\n\n    return dp_prev_row[n - 1]"}
