{"task_id": "Mbpp/272", "solution": "def rear_extract(tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list containing the last element of each tuple in the input list.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if the top-level input is not a list or any element is not a tuple.\n        ValueError: if any tuple is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuples, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of tuples\")\n\n    result = []\n    for idx, t in enumerate(tuples):\n        if not isinstance(t, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Non-tuple element encountered at index {idx}\")\n        if len(t) == 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Empty tuple encountered at index {idx}\")\n        result.append(t[-1])\n\n    return result"}
