{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(listA, listB, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists,\n    selecting one factor from each list.\n    \"\"\"\n    import heapq\n\n    if not listA or not listB or k <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Helper function using a max-heap (implemented with heapq's min-heap for negated values).\n    # Assumes 'a' and 'b' are sorted in descending order.\n    # It efficiently finds the 'count' largest products.\n    def _get_top_products_from_desc(a: list, b: list, count: int) -> list:\n        n, m = len(a), len(b)\n        if n == 0 or m == 0 or count <= 0:\n            return []\n\n        heap_entries = [(-(a[0] * b[0]), 0, 0)]\n        visited_indices = {(0, 0)}\n        output_products = []\n\n        while heap_entries and len(output_products) < count:\n            neg_prod, i, j = heapq.heappop(heap_entries)\n            output_products.append(-neg_prod)\n\n            if i + 1 < n and (i + 1, j) not in visited_indices:\n                visited_indices.add((i + 1, j))\n                heapq.heappush(heap_entries, (-(a[i + 1] * b[j]), i + 1, j))\n\n            if j + 1 < m and (i, j + 1) not in visited_indices:\n                visited_indices.add((i, j + 1))\n                heapq.heappush(heap_entries, (-(a[i] * b[j + 1]), i, j + 1))\n        return output_products\n\n    # Helper for negative products (positive * negative), finds products (negative values).\n    # Assumes a_pos sorted ascending, b_neg sorted ascending (i.e., values closer to zero first).\n    def _get_top_negative_products_from_asc_pos_asc_neg(a_pos: list, b_neg: list, count: int) -> list:\n        n, m = len(a_pos), len(b_neg)\n        if n == 0 or m == 0 or count <= 0:\n            return []\n\n        heap_entries = [(-(a_pos[0] * b_neg[0]), 0, 0)]\n        visited_indices = {(0, 0)}\n        output_products = []\n\n        while heap_entries and len(output_products) < count:\n            neg_prod, i, j = heapq.heappop(heap_entries)\n            output_products.append(-neg_prod)\n\n            if i + 1 < n and (i + 1, j) not in visited_indices:\n                visited_indices.add((i + 1, j))\n                heapq.heappush(heap_entries, (-(a_pos[i + 1] * b_neg[j]), i + 1, j))\n\n            if j + 1 < m and (i, j + 1) not in visited_indices:\n                visited_indices.add((i, j + 1))\n                heapq.heappush(heap_entries, (-(a_pos[i] * b_neg[j + 1]), i, j + 1))\n        return output_products\n\n    # Prepare lists by sign and sort for different scenarios\n    a_pos = [float(x) for x in listA if x > 0]\n    b_pos = [float(x) for x in listB if x > 0]\n    a_neg = [float(x) for x in listA if x < 0]\n    b_neg = [float(x) for x in listB if x < 0]\n\n    a_pos_desc = sorted(a_pos, reverse=True)\n    b_pos_desc = sorted(b_pos, reverse=True)\n\n    # For negative*negative positive products, sort by absolute value descending\n    a_neg_abs_desc = sorted(a_neg, key=abs, reverse=True)\n    b_neg_abs_desc = sorted(b_neg, key=abs, reverse=True)\n\n    # For positive*negative combinations (to get negative products closer to zero first)\n    a_pos_asc = sorted(a_pos)\n    b_pos_asc = sorted(b_pos)\n    a_neg_asc = sorted(a_neg)\n    b_neg_asc = sorted(b_neg)\n\n    a_has_zero = any(x == 0 for x in listA)\n    b_has_zero = any(x == 0 for x in listB)\n\n    # Use a min-heap to maintain the 'k' largest products found overall.\n    result_min_heap = []\n\n    def add_product(product_val):\n        if len(result_min_heap) < k:\n            heapq.heappush(result_min_heap, product_val)\n        elif product_val > result_min_heap[0]:\n            heapq.heapreplace(result_min_heap, product_val)\n\n    # 1. Candidate products from (Positive * Positive)\n    for prod in _get_top_products_from_desc(a_pos_desc, b_pos_desc, k):\n        add_product(prod)\n\n    # 2. Candidate products from (Negative * Negative) -> positive products\n    for prod in _get_top_products_from_desc(a_neg_abs_desc, b_neg_abs_desc, k):\n        add_product(prod)\n\n    # 3. Candidate products from (Positive * Negative) -> negative products\n    for prod in _get_top_negative_products_from_asc_pos_asc_neg(a_pos_asc, b_neg_asc, k):\n        add_product(prod)\n    for prod in _get_top_negative_products_from_asc_pos_asc_neg(b_pos_asc, a_neg_asc, k):\n        add_product(prod)\n\n    # 4. Handle zero products\n    if a_has_zero or b_has_zero:\n        add_product(0.0)\n\n    # If no candidates were added (e.g., when lists had mixed signs but candidates missed),\n    # fall back to brute-force when total combinations are small.\n    total_combinations = len(listA) * len(listB)\n    if not result_min_heap and total_combinations > 0 and total_combinations <= 10000:\n        all_products = [float(x) * float(y) for x in listA for y in listB]\n        all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n        return all_products[:k]\n\n    final_products = sorted(result_min_heap, reverse=True)\n    return final_products[:k]"}
