{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "from decimal import Decimal\ndef first_Digit(num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first significant digit of a number, ignoring sign and leading zeros.\n    Handles integers, floats, and numeric strings.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_value = None\n    if isinstance(num, int):\n        s_value = str(abs(num))\n    elif isinstance(num, float):\n        # Convert float to a precise decimal string representation to avoid scientific notation.\n        s_value = str(Decimal(str(num)))\n    elif isinstance(num, str):\n        # Parse numeric string via Decimal for robust handling and then stringify.\n        s_value = str(Decimal(num.strip()))\n\n    # Remove sign, decimal point, and leading zeros to get the canonical digit string.\n    temp_s = s_value.lstrip('+-')\n    temp_s = temp_s.replace('.', '')\n    normalized_digits_str = temp_s.lstrip('0')\n\n    # If the number was 0 or 0.0 (or composed only of zeros), the normalized string will be empty.\n    if not normalized_digits_str:\n        return 0\n\n    # Return the first digit as an integer.\n    return int(normalized_digits_str[0])"}
