{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first n natural numbers using a closed-form formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be >= 0\")\n\n    # The sum of the first n natural numbers (T) is n * (n + 1) // 2.\n    # The sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers is T * T.\n    # The required difference is (T * T) - T = T * (T - 1).\n    t = (n * (n + 1)) // 2\n    return t * (t - 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs in a list whose XOR value is odd.\n    An XOR is odd if one number is odd and the other is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num % 2 != 0:  # Check if number is odd\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    even_count = len(numbers) - odd_count\n\n    return odd_count * even_count"}
